 ],
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.05,
   "text": "The next evening, Sam tries something small. The *mug* is dirty again."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.1,
   "end": 8.65,
   "text": "He sees it. He leaves it on purpose."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.7,
   "end": 15.75,
   "text": "He sits down and sets a *timer*. Three minutes. Rest first, while the thing is still undone."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.8,
   "end": 20.85,
   "text": "At first, it's quiet. Then, around the thirty-second mark, there it is."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.9,
   "end": 25.15,
   "text": "A thought: I should really also... Sam almost gets up."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.2,
   "end": 33.05,
   "text": "Here's step one. He notices the thought and doesn't obey it. He just says to himself: there you are."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.1,
   "end": 38.55,
   "text": "The urge rises. It sits there. And a little later, it gets weaker."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.6,
   "end": 43.35,
   "text": "He didn't have to fight it. He just didn't follow it."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.4,
   "end": 49.65,
   "text": "Step two. He gives the *mug* a *plan*. Not a clean *mug*, just a *plan*."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.7,
   "end": 52.75,
   "text": "This is straight from that *2011* research."
  },
  {
   "start": 52.8,
   "end": 58.25,
   "text": "He picks up his phone and types: Mug, sink, tomorrow morning, before coffee."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.3,
   "end": 64.55,
   "text": "When people made a specific *plan* for an *unfinished* goal, the mental noise went away."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.6,
   "end": 71.65,
   "text": "They didn't have to finish the task. They only had to decide how it would get done."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.7,
   "end": 77.15,
   "text": "Sam feels it. The *mug* is still dirty. But the *tab* is closed."
  },
  {
   "start": 77.2,
   "end": 82.65,
   "text": "Step three. He talks to himself the way he'd talk to a friend."
  },
  {
   "start": 82.7,
   "end": 88.55,
   "text": "Not you lazy idiot. More like: you worked all day, one episode is fine."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.6,
   "end": 95.35,
   "text": "Studies on self-compassion link it with fewer symptoms of depression in people going through hard times,"
  },
  {
   "start": 95.4,
   "end": 98.95,
   "text": "and it helps buffer the sting of failure."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.0,
   "end": 104.45,
   "text": "Sam's evening is much smaller than that. But the idea is the same."
  },
  {
   "start": 104.5,
   "end": 109.25,
   "text": "Kindness isn't a reward. It's what makes it easier to function."
  },
  {
   "start": 109.3,
   "end": 116.35,
   "text": "Step four. If the *timer* goes off and he still wants to do something, fine. He can."
  },
  {
   "start": 116.4,
   "end": 121.15,
   "text": "But now it's a choice, not an escape from a feeling."
  },
  {
   "start": 121.2,
   "end": 127.05,
   "text": "He looks at the *timer*. Three minutes have passed. He didn't die. Nobody called."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.1,
   "end": 132.55,
   "text": "The package is still by the door, and the world is still standing."
  }
 ]
}